var ROUTE=[["Narshe — prologue",1,"",["Ymir: attack the HEAD only (1,600 HP). The Shell has 50,000 HP and cannot be killed — hitting it triggers Megavolt on the whole party","Both Ymir entries register from a single win — no need to kill the Shell","No lightning attacks — Ymir absorbs them and heals","Guard Leader Rage is here — the first of your nine combat-critical Rages","STRIP MOG DURING THE MOOGLE DEFENCE — the menu is reachable between waves. Unequip BOTH his Mythril Spear AND Mythril Shield there; once the sequence ends he is gone with them","That spear is Edgar's free weapon at Figaro Castle; miss it and you buy one instead","Mines chests UPGRADE — leave all three for the World of Ruin","Grab the beginner's classroom chests; the Silver Lobo chest is a fight","Terra starts at 3 and should STAY there — no stat espers exist yet, so any level now is wasted","Her low level also drags the party average down, so every later recruit joins lower — including BANON, which is why the Lethe River is hard. That is a real cost, and worth it."],[],[0,59,1],[0,1],"",null,null,null,["Fight the forced Magitek Armor battles through town to the Narshe Mines entrance (back row for everyone, no equipment changes possible yet)","Save at the first Save Point, then push north to Ymir","Ymir fight: attack only the Head (1,600 HP); never target the Shell (50,000 HP, absorbs Lightning, counters any hit including stray AoE with ~65 dmg Megavolt)","After the scene, name Terra and Locke; grab the Elixir near the front door, then head out to a second mine entrance","In the narrow one-tile corridor before the Moogle room, open the menu and strip Terra's Mythril Knife and Buckler — hand them to Locke","Take the tutorial if offered, then during the Moogle Defense open the menu between waves and strip Mog's Mythril Spear AND Mythril Shield","Fight through to the Guard Leader (learn the Guard Leader/Wind Slash Rage here); Locke can steal a Mythril Knife from him","Visit the Adventuring School (beginner's classroom) chests, including the Silver Lobo Monster-in-a-Box","Leave Narshe for the World Map"]],["North Figaro — plains & desert",1,"",["Leaf Bunny, Darkwind, Sand Ray, Alacran roam here — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1. Check them off from either place; ticking one ticks both"],[],[22,23],[],"",null,null,null,["Cross the grass/forest/desert on the way to Figaro Castle","Fight/steal from Alacran, Darkwind, Leaf Bunny, Sand Ray as encountered","Try to meet at least one Alacran (its Stop-inflicting Rage becomes very useful soon)","Continue to the castle in the middle of the desert"]],["Figaro Castle",1,"",["Basement chests are World of Ruin only — don't hunt for them yet"],[],[],[2],"",[["Noiseblaster",500,"EDGAR — full price; no discount possible yet",null],["Bioblaster",750,"EDGAR — full price; needed later for the Imperial Elite",null],["Hold off on consumables",0,"what you have will reach South Figaro",null],["Give Edgar Mog's Mythril Spear",0,"free, unequipped back in the Narshe mines — no need to buy him a weapon",null]],null,null,["Name Edgar, then explore the throne room area","Loot the Tool Shop area chests (Potion, Antidote) and buy Bioblaster + Noiseblaster (Auto Crossbow already given)","Loot the Item Shop's Gold Needle chest and the tower's Phoenix Down chest","Speak to the High Priestess, then Edgar, then Kefka to advance","Fight the forced Magitek Armor back-attack pincer","Ride the Chocobo/castle to the southeastern desert cave to reach South Figaro Cave"]],["South Figaro Cave — first trek",1,"Entering Returner Hideout",["Turn encounters ON — Foper, Urok and Hornet must each be fought at least once on THIS trek. Boarding the raft afterward swaps the cave's encounter table and they're gone for good","All three chests UPGRADE — leave all three. Two keep improving into the World of Ruin; the west-end chest reaches its final X-Potion on the Locke and Celes trek"],["g1"],[2],[3],"once",null,null,null,["Turn encounters ON before entering","Fight through Foper/Hornet/Urok — Fire and Auto Crossbow work well","Auto-heal at the Recovery Spring on the first screen","At the first junction, skip the west Ether chest (upgrades later)","At the next junction, skip the east Ether chest and the Phoenix Down chest near the stairs (both upgrade later)","Exit southeast to South Figaro town"]],["South Figaro — town",1,"",["Sabin's house bucket is gone in the World of Ruin","Outdoor barrels/crates upgrade — but three get WORSE. Check the Chests list.","Weapon upgrades are OPTIONAL for Edgar, Sabin, Shadow and Cyan — Tools, Blitz, Throw and Bushido all ignore weapon power","So spend the gil on Terra and Locke, who actually swing theirs","Belmodar, Unseelie and Mu roam BOTH sides of Mt. Kolts — you get a second chance outside the Returner Hideout","Belmodar COUNTERS any Magic command with Megavolt — hit it physically only","Steal Mythril Claws from Belmodar (rare) — Sabin joins at Mt. Kolts and uses claws. Two is ideal","Unseelie carries a Buckler worth stealing","Free beds and a Potion in the bucket at the house due north of town","Belmodar, Unseelie, Mu are also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1 — check them off from either place"],[],[24],[4,5,6],"",[["Great Sword",800,"TERRA — not Edgar, who already has Mog's free Mythril Spear",null],["Mythril Sword",450,"LOCKE",null],["Nothing for EDGAR",0,"he keeps Mog's Mythril Spear from the prologue — and Tools ignore weapon power entirely",null],["Heavy Shield",400,"EDGAR and LOCKE — buy two",null],["Plumed Hat",250,"EDGAR, TERRA, LOCKE, plus a spare for SABIN — buy four","Sabin"],["Cotton Robe",200,"TERRA",null],["Kenpo Gi",250,"LOCKE",null],["Buckler",200,"spare for SABIN, who joins at Mt. Kolts","Sabin"],["Sprint Shoes",1500,"optional quality-of-life only — Simmeh calls no relic here critical",null],["Potions ×25",1250,"party stock",null],["Phoenix Down ×5",2500,"party stock",null],["Antidote ×3",150,"more if you plan extra Mt. Kolts encounters",null],["Tent ×1–2",2400,"party stock",null],["DON'T buy status relics",0,"Hyper Wrist and Hermes Sandals are FREE in the rich man's basement, with 3,000 gil",null],["DON'T overstock",0,"Figaro Castle sells the same consumables at half price later with Edgar leading",null]],null,null,["Explore the rich man's house — Phoenix Down barrel outside, hidden passage behind the upstairs bookcase to a Hyper Wrist + Hermes Sandals cell, and a clock room with 500/1000/1500 Gil chests","Grab the free-standing items that never change (X-Potion between the shops, Green Cherry, Teleport Stone) and leave the ones that upgrade later (Eyedrops, Gold Needle, and the two Potions)","Shop: Great Sword for Terra, Plumed Hats/Heavy Shields/Cotton Robe/Kenpo Gi from the Armor Shop, Jeweled Ring + Star Pendants from the Relic Shop","Head to the South Figaro region: fight/steal from Belmodar (physical only — it counters Magic with Megavolt), Unseelie (steal the Buckler), and Mu","Rest for free and grab the Potion at the house north of town","Head northeast to the mountain trail and save before Mt. Kolts"]],["Mt. Kolts",1,"",["Trillium Rage here — one of your nine combat-critical ones","Two chests sit behind hidden passages, south-east and north-east of the main cave","MISSABLE SCENE: after beating Vargas, walk back to South Figaro and talk to Duncan's wife. Entering the Returner Hideout locks it out forever","Equip Edgar with the Gigas Glove (here) and Hyper Wrist (South Figaro basement) BEFORE Vargas","VARGAS PHASE 1: he cannot be targeted until both Ipoohs die — not even by all-target attacks","Ipoohs have 360 HP each and are weak to Fire. Terra casts Fire on one at a time; Edgar uses Auto Crossbow","Gale Cut hits the whole party for ~50, so keep everyone above that. Terra heals, she does not need to damage","VARGAS PHASE 2: you never need to deplete his HP — 720 damage total makes Sabin appear","Edgar's Bioblaster (140+) is your best tool; roughly five or six turns","PIXEL REMASTER TRAP: Raging Fist does NOTHING until Sabin's tutorial dialogue has fired","So act once with something else (Aura Cannon or a plain attack), let the tutorial trigger, THEN Raging Fist","Gale Cut no longer ignores Split Damage in PR — it does 100+ to a solo Sabin who has about 132 HP","You CANNOT save once the battle starts — quicksave on the field before triggering Vargas","So a Sabin death costs the whole fight: both Ipoohs and the 720 damage again","Sabin gets roughly two turns before a second Gale Cut kills him. Spend turn one triggering the tutorial, turn two on Raging Fist","Phase 2 also opens with Doom Fist, inflicting a separate Doom countdown (~60 sec) that is a straight Game Over on its own if it expires — don't dawdle even if Gale Cut looks survivable","Vargas and both Ipoohs are separate bestiary entries","Locke can steal a rare Mythril Claw from Vargas","Clear all four chests before you leave","Zaghrem, Gorgias, Cirpius aren't required here, but are listed too in case they turn up while you're farming Trillium — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1"],[],[25,60],[7],"wob",null,null,null,["Fight through Cirpius/Gorgias/Zaghrem/Trillium/Spritzer on the way up (learn the Trillium Rage)","Grab the two hidden-passage chests (Main Gauche area, Gigas Glove) and the two Tent chests","Optional: return to South Figaro to trigger Duncan's wife's missable scene about Sabin before proceeding (locked out once you enter the Returner Hideout)","Equip Edgar with the Gigas Glove and Hyper Wrist, heal fully, then approach Vargas","Phase 1: kill both Ipoohs first (Vargas is untargetable until they're dead) — Fire from Terra, Auto Crossbow/Bioblaster from Edgar, keep everyone above ~50 HP for Gale Cut","Once 720 total damage has been dealt, the scene triggers and Sabin takes over solo","Phase 2: act once (Aura Cannon or a normal attack) to make Sabin's Blitz tutorial fire, THEN input Raging Fist to end the fight","Loot the Tent chest past Vargas, then continue to the Returner Hideout"]],["Returner Hideout",1,"Leaving the hideout",["GEAR RULE FOR ALL THREE SCENARIOS: strip a departing character at the last point you still control movement, NOT when the scenario 'ends'. Cutscenes lock the menu","The strip between Mt. Kolts and the hideout has NO new enemies — same Belmodar, Unseelie and Mu","Last chance for those three if you skipped them near South Figaro","First shop selling Hi-Potions — stock up here","BANON: say YES for the Gauntlet. Yes on the first, second OR third ask all give it — saying no first costs nothing","But do NOT talk to the Returner in the storage room after saying no — he hands you the Genji Glove and Banon then withholds the Gauntlet","You can only ever have one of the two","Saying no three times only changes the cutscene: Terra's introspection replaces the strategy meeting","You get a Genji Glove from a chest in the Cave to the Sealed Gate anyway; the Gauntlet appears at only two other points, both far later","CORRECTED PR NOTE: the Genji Glove is still the stronger relic here — PR only fixed a bug where its dual-wield penalty was wrongly hitting single-weapon use, which nerfed (not buffed) its old numbers; the Gauntlet was never touched. Take the Gauntlet anyway for a different reason: it's strictly quantity-limited, while Genji Glove is farmable later (Cave to the Sealed Gate chest, Metamorphose) — so this is a scarcity call, not a power one","Nine containers here, none available in the World of Ruin","STRIP LOCKE COMPLETELY before accepting Banon's request — that's the actual swap point, not the raft itself; he leaves for his own scenario the moment you accept and takes everything he's still wearing with him","The raft party needs that gear for Ultros"],["g2"],[],[8],"wob",[["Hi-Potion",0,"FIRST place in the game that sells them — stock up hard",null],["Phoenix Down / Antidote / Tent",0,"item shop only; there are no relics or equipment here",null],["FREE INN",0,"the inn here costs nothing. Rest to full before boarding the raft — Banon starts the Ultros fight at whatever HP he has now",null]],null,null,["Explore the storeroom area for Air Knife/Phoenix Down/Knight's Code chests, an Antidote/Ether, and a hidden-passage White Cape","Visit the meeting room east of the entrance: talk to Sabin, grab the Green Cherry pot, note the first Hi-Potions for sale","Return to Edgar's room and open the Hi-Potion chest","Talk to everyone, then speak to Banon just outside the exit","Before accepting his request, strip Locke of all his gear (it returns to the shared pool)","Choose Gauntlet (accept) or Genji Glove (decline, then talk to the Returner in the storeroom) — you can only ever get one this way","Accept Banon's request to trigger the scene where he replaces Locke in the party","Head south and board the raft"]],["Lethe River",1,"",["ULTROS #1 — Banon must survive. If he is KO'd it is an instant Game Over, not a normal loss","Put EVERYONE in the back row, Banon included. Tentacle is physical, so the row halves it","Banon's Pray command (renamed from 'Health' pre-PR) heals the whole party — he should be casting it most turns, not attacking","IF BANON IS TOO FRAGILE: you can safely level HIM alone. Set EXP to 4x, KO Terra, Edgar and Sabin, and let Banon finish fights solo — KO'd characters gain no EXP, so only he levels","This is safe ONLY because Banon leaves at the end of his own scenario, before Celes, Cyan and Gau join. Do Terra/Edgar/Banon's scenario FIRST and his level never enters their averaging","Set EXP back to 0x the moment he is comfortable","Sabin is swept away after Ultros, which triggers THE SCENARIO SPLIT here","ORDER: Terra/Edgar/Banon first, then Locke, then Sabin","Terra's is easiest and lets you strip gear risk-free; Sabin's is longest and hardest, so it should inherit everything","Lesser Lopros, Nautiloid, Exocite aren't required here, but are listed too — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1"],[],[26,61],[],"wob",null,null,null,["At the first intersection, go left; use the Save Point cave","At the next intersection, go left again (or grind on the loop if desired); use the second Save Point","Ultros fight: keep everyone (especially Banon) in the Back Row / Defending, track his 3-turn attack script, and be ready to have Banon Defend at full HP right before his Banon-targeting Tentacle","Heal Terra when Ultros' scripted 10-second attack targets her, then have her nuke with Fire","After the win, watch the scenes — Sabin is swept away and the party splits into three scenarios","Do the scenarios in order: Terra/Edgar/Banon, then Locke, then Sabin"]],["Terra / Edgar / Banon scenario — Narshe",1,"",["DO THIS SCENARIO FIRST — easiest, and you can strip gear for the other two with no risk","The river drops you east of Narshe; the guards block the gate, so go back through the mines","Valeor and Wild Rat only appear in this west mines corridor, but it's walkable again for the rest of the World of Balance — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1","SECURITY CHECKPOINT: on entering, a light TRACES the correct route across the room — watch it, then walk the same path. There is no fixed map to memorise; the game shows you every time","IF YOU STRAY: eight lights surround you — SEVEN BLUE, ONE ORANGE/GOLD. Face the GOLD one and interact. They scatter and nothing happens","Miss the gold one and you fight two undead, then get sent back to the room's start. No progress lost, just time","CORRECTED: the strays have NO bestiary entries, but Darkside, Specter and Eukaryote ARE valid Rages obtainable ONLY here — stray on purpose at least once if you're going for a full Rage list. No bestiary cost either way, since these three never get one","No random encounters in this room at all, and in the World of Ruin the checkpoint stops triggering entirely","Past the checkpoint the Moogle room opens — the Rune Blade chest UPGRADES to a Ribbon, so leave it","Healing pot next to Banon (Pixel Remaster addition)","STRIP TERRA AND EDGAR COMPLETELY — relics included — BEFORE you talk to Arvis. Talking to him ends the scenario immediately and there is no menu after that","Anything still worn by Terra or Edgar is locked to them and unavailable to Locke and Sabin","Only then talk to Arvis to end the scenario"],[],[5],[9],"once",null,null,null,["Cross the North Figaro region back to Narshe (Valeor/Wild Rat only appear in the west mines corridor here)","Enter through the secret passage west of the Adventuring School","Fight through the Wererat/Bandit cave, then the Valeor/Wild Rat mine","In the security checkpoint room, follow the traced light path; if caught, face the single gold/orange light among the seven blue ones to escape without a fight","Optionally stray on purpose at least once to fight the wrong-path encounters and pick up the Darkside/Specter/Eukaryote Rages","Skip the Rune Blade chest (it upgrades to a Ribbon later) and continue past the other chests/Save Point","Before talking to Arvis, strip Edgar's Gigas Glove, Terra's White Cape, and any relics/Bandanas needed later","Talk to Arvis to end the scenario"]],["Locke's scenario — South Figaro",1,"Scenario end",["Equip Locke from the shared pool first — he is solo and fragile. Main Gauche, Mythril Shield, Bandana, Kenpo Gi, plus White Cape and Hermes Sandals if free","Do NOT use the Kutan glitch","LEAVE the Thunder Rod — that chest becomes a HERO'S RING in the World of Ruin. Breaking the rod one-shots Tunnel Armor, but the ring is the better prize and you are guaranteed a return trip","TAKE the X-Potion (west end of the main cave) — it is already at its final value and never upgrades again","TUNNEL ARMOR without the rod: Celes uses RUNIC every single turn to eat its magic, Locke attacks, Potions to heal. Long but not dangerous","Re-select Runic only AFTER it absorbs something — choosing any other command for Celes drops the stance","Hermes Sandals on Celes for auto-Haste so she can keep Runic up between its casts","HEAVY ARMOR blocks passages in town, but solo Locke will almost certainly lose. Skip it here — the entry is also available at the Battle of Narshe","Cartagra, Acrophies, Gold Bear appear only on the SECOND cave trek","The cave swaps its encounter table between treks — those three only appear on the second pass","STRIP LOCKE AND CELES COMPLETELY BEFORE ENGAGING TUNNEL ARMOR — this is your LAST menu access. You cannot change equipment during the fight, and the scenario ends straight after it"],[],[3,4],[16,17],"once",null,null,null,["Equip Locke from the shared pool and move him to the Front Row","Work through the disguise puzzle (steal a Merchant outfit, get the Cider from the Pub basement Merchant, learn the password 'Courage') to reach the Old Man's basement passage — do NOT use the Kutan/Moghan glitch to skip it","Recruit Celes in the secret passage, gear her up, and grab the Old Clock Key from the sleeping guard","Loot the storage-room chests (Iron Armor, Heavy Shield, Great Sword, Hi-Ether, X-Potion, Ribbon, Earring) and unlock the clock door","Exit to the World Map, then re-enter South Figaro Cave for the second trek (new enemies: Acrophies, Cartagra, Gold Bear)","Leave the Thunder Rod chest for its World of Ruin Hero's Ring upgrade; take the already-final X-Potion","Before the boss, strip transferable gear for Sabin's scenario (this is the last menu access) — fight Tunnel Armor with Celes on Runic every available turn and Locke attacking/healing"]],["Sabin's scenario — overworld to the Imperial Camp",1,"",["The walk from the starting house to the desert patch crosses grass and forest carrying Stray Cat, Aepyornis, Nettlehopper and Chippirabbit — this is where that encounter group actually lives, not inside the camp itself","STRAY CAT is missable and Gau's strongest physical Rage (Cat Scratch, x4 damage) — worth prioritizing here since every formation you fight elsewhere first only dilutes the Veldt pool","Aepyornis, Nettlehopper and Chippirabbit are NOT time-critical — this terrain stays walkable, and flyable once you have the airship, for the rest of the World of Balance, so those three are also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1","All four are World of Balance only — the WoR version of this ground swaps in Tumbleweed/Crawler/Sprinter/Lycaon instead, confirmed against this tracker's own WoR overworld entry for the region","GRASS tends to favor Aepyornis and Chippirabbit; FOREST tends to favor Nettlehopper and Stray Cat — but this is a tendency, not a hard split. Player reports (and PR guides hedging with “usually”) confirm Stray Cat can show up on grass too","The odds above come from an older console datamine — Pixel Remaster may have shuffled these formations, so treat tile type as a lean, not a rule","If Chippirabbit specifically is still missing, grass is still the better bet, just not a guarantee"],[],[6,63],[],"wob",null,null,null,["Recruit Shadow from the traveling merchant outside the starting house (buy Shurikens for Throw)","Cross the grass/forest terrain toward the desert, fighting Stray Cat/Aepyornis/Nettlehopper/Chippirabbit as encountered","Prioritize meeting at least one Stray Cat here — its Cat Scratch Rage is confirmed as the strongest single-target Rage available for a long while","Save before entering the 'desert,' which is actually the Imperial Camp"]],["Sabin's scenario — Imperial Camp",1,"Leaving the camp",["Equip Sabin from the pool before starting — anything still worn by Locke or Celes is unavailable to him","Kick the first chest for the Doberman fight — Veldt appearance is mandatory","Open the Satellite box for Green Berets","The Satellite in the tent drops a Green Beret — farm the other three later on the Veldt"],["g4"],[7],[10],"once",null,null,["OPTIONAL: Shadow offers to join Sabin here for free — worth taking. He leaves automatically at Baren Falls either way, so there's no downside to accepting"],["Equip Sabin from the shared pool (Locke/Celes gear is now available if done in the recommended order)","Name and take control of Cyan; fight the Leader for a Black Belt (reset if it drops a Phoenix Down instead)","Kick (not hit) the tent chest to force the mandatory Doberman fight — this is the only place to ever meet it","Grab the Barrier Ring by jumping down behind the west tent","Open the Mythril Glove chest, then fight Satellite for the Star Pendant/Green Beret — missable here, but repeatable on the Veldt afterward for more Green Berets","Provoke Kefka three times (he flees each time) while clearing the surrounding Imperial Soldiers/Templars","Leave the camp for good"]],["Sabin's scenario — Doma Castle",1,"",["CYAN joins here","TWO Cyan segments here. FIRST is the siege: you control Cyan outside the gates and the objective is the CAPTAIN (#36)","The wall-climbing troopers all start the SAME 2x Imperial Soldier fight — one is enough for the entry, the rest give nothing","Menu is open in that segment: equip Cyan from the shared pool. He keeps whatever you give him when he joins","SECOND, after Kefka poisons the water: the REMEDY POT is the only obtainable item in the whole castle. Every other treasure is blocked off","It is in the waiting area under the stairs — carpeted stairs south of the throne room, then the south-east room, pot on the right. Both bottom doors lead there","The top-right door is a dead end — Cyan just steps back out saying \"Here too...\"","GRAB IT FIRST. The upper-right door past the throne room is his family, and that ends the segment on the spot","Not a hard loss — Cyan's Dream carries the same treasures, obtainable in one location or the other"],[],[],[11],"wob",null,null,null,["Control switches to Cyan outside the gates for the siege segment — the objective is the Captain (bestiary #36), not the rank-and-file soldiers","Fight one of the 2x Imperial Soldier groups if you want the bestiary/Rage entry (optional; every soldier group is identical), then beat the Captain to end the siege","Menu is open on Cyan here — equip him from the shared pool before he departs with Sabin/Shadow","Control returns to Sabin/Shadow in the Imperial Camp; explore, then Kefka poisons Doma's water and flees to the castle","Control switches back to Cyan inside the castle — go down to the throne room and watch the king die","Go through either of the two bottom doors past the throne room (both lead to the same room) and take the Remedy from the pot on the right","Do NOT enter the upper-right door yet if you still want other loot in that pass — it triggers the family scene and ends the segment on the spot","Enter the upper-right door when ready: Cyan finds his wife and son, swears revenge, and the segment ends, sending him to the Imperial Camp to join the party"]],["Sabin's scenario — Phantom Forest",1,"",["Ghost Rage here — combat-critical","Poplium isn't required here — it's also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1"],[],[8,65],[],"wob",null,null,null,["Enter the forest southeast of Doma Castle with Sabin (Cyan and, if he's stuck around, Shadow)","Fight through Ghost/Poplium encounters — this is the only source for the Ghost Rage in this scenario","Always take the exit at the top of the screen; other exits loop you back","Step on the Recovery Spring tile to auto-heal before continuing","Reach the wrecked train at the far side of the forest and board it to start the Phantom Train segment"]],["Sabin's scenario — Phantom Train",1,"Leaving the train",["Seven entries, not the two Simmeh routes","Oversoul Rage — combat-critical","The chest Siegfried steals can never be recovered"],["g5"],[9],[12],"once",null,null,null,["Board the train; Shadow can be revived/used again safely now that he's trapped aboard (he won't flee mid-train)","Work through the cars, picking up the Tent, Earring, second Tent, Phoenix Down x2, and Sniper Eye chests along the way","Optionally accept a temporary Ghost ally at one of the early cars (he leaves automatically before the locomotive)","Open the chest in the fourth suite when Siegfried appears — he steals its contents regardless of the fight's outcome, and it can never be recovered","Defeat the Apparition monster-in-a-box for a Hyper Wrist","Reach the locomotive, flip the correct pressure valves, then fight the Phantom Train boss — this is the only place Oversoul is learnable","Watch the Cyan family cutscene and exit to the overworld"]],["Sabin's scenario — Baren Falls",1,"",["Rhizopas boss","SHADOW LEAVES HERE — if he joined this scenario as a guest, he departs at the very start of this scene and takes whatever he's wearing with him until he's re-recruited at the Kohlingen tavern","STRIP SHADOW'S EQUIPMENT before triggering Baren Falls — the Phantom Train is safe for this, but your true last menu access is actually the field screen right after leaving the train, before the dive","You land on the Veldt and meet Gau, who runs off — see the next stop"],[],[10],[],"once",null,null,null,["Immediately after leaving the Phantom Train you land on a field screen with full menu access — this, not the train itself, is your true last chance to strip Shadow's gear","Walk east into the cave and head toward the falls","Dive down the falls: fight waves of Opinicus Fish for about 60 seconds","Rhizopas appears after the wave timer — burst it down with strong single-target hits (Fang, Aura Cannon) before it gets off El Nino","Shadow automatically leaves the party the moment you reach the falls, taking whatever he's still wearing","You land on the Veldt and meet Gau, who runs off — proceed to the next stop"]],["Sabin's scenario — Mobliz",1,"",["Elixir in the mailman's clock — this one is still here in the World of Ruin"],[],[],[13],"",[["Mythril Claw",800,"SABIN",null],["Kotetsu",800,"CYAN",null],["Magus Hat",600,"buy now for much later — Terra/Strago","Strago"],["White Cape ×2 extra",10000,"you want three in total",null],["Dried Meat",150,"required to recruit GAU on the Veldt","Gau"],["Green Berets are FREE",0,"Satellites in Veldt group 8 always drop one — farm two",null]],null,null,["Enter Mobliz","Buy at least one Dried Meat from the item shop — the only source in the game, and required to recruit Gau","Grab the Elixir from the clock in the mailman's house","Head back out to the Veldt"]],["Sabin's scenario — The Veldt (recruiting Gau)",1,"",["You land here straight after Baren Falls and Gau runs off — you cannot recruit him yet","Buy Dried Meat in Mobliz first, then come back and drop it to recruit him","Farm Rages now: this is the only Veldt access until much later","Farm Green Berets from Satellite drops — four total is the target","Gau's join level is your PARTY AVERAGE plus a fixed +2 bonus — the +2 is fixed, the resulting number isn't. It lands around 7 on this route's usual pace, but moves if your average does, and it's been dragging every later join (Shadow included) up ever since"],[],[],[],"",null,null,null,["Return to the Veldt with Dried Meat in inventory (you land here first without it and can't recruit him yet)","Fight formations until Gau appears saying he's hungry","Use the Dried Meat item on him instead of attacking — he joins after the ensuing dialogue","Before leaving, farm the Satellite formation for extra Green Berets and fight other formations for Rages — this is the only Veldt access for a long stretch","Continue on to the Serpent Trench"]],["Sabin's scenario — Serpent Trench",1,"",["Anguiform Rage — combat-critical, wanted later for Cranes","Aspiran Rage — combat-critical, wanted for Ultros at the Opera House","Fighting them HERE only unlocks their Veldt formation — Gau still has to fight that same formation once ON THE VELDT to actually learn the Rage. Make a Veldt stop before the Opera House or Aspiran will not be usable yet","Not available in the World of Ruin — take both chests","Actinian isn't required here — it's also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1, as long as you fly the raft entrance again before triggering the Floating Continent"],[],[11,64],[14],"wob",null,null,null,["Board the raft; it's a mostly-automatic ride with two branch-point choices","Pick the right fork at both decision points to reach the two side caves","First cave: grab the X-Potion chest","Second cave: climb the stairs, hit the switch to drain the flooded section, drop through the hole, and grab the Green Beret chest","Fight Anguiform/Aspiran/Actinian formations along the way to seed their Veldt pools — remember this only unlocks the Veldt formation, Gau still needs to fight that formation on an actual Veldt visit to learn the Rage","Ride out to Nikeah to end the trench segment"]],["Sabin's scenario — Nikeah",1,"Boarding the ship",["Elixir in the Inn clock","LAST STOP of Sabin's scenario — boarding the ship at the docks ends it and everyone meets up at Narshe","Shop before you board; this is your last chance to spend before the Narshe battle"],[],[],[15],"",[["Silk Robe",600,"CELES — the only notable item in Nikeah",null],["Mythril Spear",800,"MOG uses spears and joins much later","Mog"]],null,null,["Enter Nikeah","Grab the Elixir from the clock in the Inn","Shop for any last gear/items — this is your final chance before the Battle of Narshe","Head to the docks and board the ship to end Sabin's scenario"]],["Battle of Narshe",1,"Defeating Kefka",["All 7 available characters (Terra, Locke, Edgar, Sabin, Celes, Cyan, Gau) get assigned to a team and DO fight — nobody sits this one out","Main combat team does 100% of the heavy lifting and MUST include Celes and Gau — add Edgar and Sabin, then strip Locke's gear onto them","Second and third teams fight too — just weaker soldier waves blocking their own path to Banon, not a boss — so give them the leftover gear","Cut through the enemies — do not dodge them","HEAVY ARMOR (#24) comes from the BROWN soldier squads here — this is the safe place to take that entry rather than solo Locke in South Figaro. It is the rarer of the two brown formations, so do not rush Kefka","No spell-casting Rages against Heavy Armor while Celes is in the party — she triggers its Magitek Barrier, which grants it Protect and Reflect. Use defence-ignoring physicals (Raging Fist, Fang) instead","Without Celes present it is weak to Lightning and Water","Treasure house chests open up here"],["g6"],[12],[18],"once",[["Weapon and armour upgrades",0,"first time Narshe's shops are usable — big jump over scenario gear",null],["Barrier Ring",500,"Shell when critically wounded, plus Magic +2",null],["Mythril Shield",1200,"front-line upgrade",null],["Silk Robe",600,"CELES",null],["Don't buy an Earring or Thief's Bracer yet",0,"both are free from the same Narshe treasure-house chest, but it's still locked — it doesn't open until AFTER the Magitek Factory. Buy here only if you need one before then",null],["Hold consumables",0,"Figaro Castle is half price with Edgar leading",null]],null,["MUST: Celes + Gau on the main team","RECOMMENDED: add Edgar + Sabin to round it out","Locke CAN fight if you keep him — he's just the weakest link, so his gear is better spent on the four above"],["At the save point, assign all 7 available characters (Terra, Locke, Edgar, Sabin, Celes, Cyan, Gau) across three teams and equip everyone — save Green Berets for Celes/Terra last","Build the main team around Celes + Gau + Edgar, with Terra or Sabin filling the fourth slot; give it your best gear","Send the other two teams to intercept soldier waves (Locke solo is popular for repeatable Steals against the runner enemy)","Fight through the green (Corporal/Hunting Hound) and brown (Fidor/Heavy Armor) soldier squads rather than dodging them — you need at least one of each for bestiary/Rage entries, and Heavy Armor is the rarer brown formation so don't rush","Against Heavy Armor, avoid magic/spell Rages if Celes is present (she triggers Magitek Barrier, granting it Protect+Reflect) — use defense-ignoring physicals instead; without Celes it's just weak to Lightning/Water","Defeat the Hell's Rider commander blocking the final approach","Speak to Kefka to trigger the boss fight and defeat/flee him to end the battle"]],["Kohlingen & region",1,"",["House at Dragon's Neck Hero's Ring is gone in the World of Ruin","Fossil Dragon and the plains/forest quintet — Vulture, Iron Fist, Bloodfang, Rock Wasp, Paraladia — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1","SHADOW is optional from here on — grab him whenever you run into him rather than saving it for a specific stop. Guaranteed for 3,000 gil at the Kohlingen tavern — this is his only free-roam recruit point in the World of Balance. CORRECTED: the South Figaro bar sighting is name-only, not a recruit point — you can't actually hire him there","Once he's in: SLEEPING AT INNS has a 50% chance each time to trigger one of his 4 backstory dreams (a 5th plays automatically later in the story) — keep resting at the same inn to cycle through them. Doesn't work at free/scripted beds like Figaro Castle or Thamasa"],[],[27,28],[19,20],"",null,null,null,["Explore Kohlingen: grab the Green Beret chest and the Elixir from the clock in Rachel's house","Visit the House at Dragon's Neck for the Hero's Ring in the pot (World of Balance only — the house is gone in the World of Ruin)","Recruit Shadow at the tavern for 3,000 gil if you want him now (the only guaranteed recruit point in this area)","If he's in, rest at inns repeatedly to roll his 50%-per-rest chance at one of his 4 backstory dreams (doesn't work at scripted/free beds like Figaro Castle or Thamasa)","Sweep the plains/forest quintet (Vulture, Iron Fist, Bloodfang, Rock Wasp, Paraladia) and Fossil Dragon if doing them now rather than during Act 1 Cleanup"]],["Jidoor",1,"",["The Auction House is here, but it's LOCKED until you have the Blackjack (after the Magitek Factory) — nothing to buy yet, tracked at Narshe, the return"],[],[],[21],"",[["Earring",5000,"magic boost, stacks if two characters wear one",null],["Sniper Eye",3000,"physicals never miss",null],["Peace Ring",3000,"blocks berserk + confusion",null],["Ninja Gear",1100,"Shadow","Shadow"],["White Dress",2200,"women's armour — also fits Terra and Celes","Relm"]],null,null,["Walk through Jidoor","Note the Auction House is locked — it opens only after the Blackjack is obtained (post-Magitek Factory), so there's nothing to buy yet","Continue on toward Zozo"]],["Zozo",1,"",["CLOCK PUZZLE — the answer is 6:10:50. Every thug in Zozo lies about the time, so the hints are worthless","The clock is on the GROUND floor of the building with the bed icon. Reward: the Chainsaw, an Edgar Tool","Gobbledygook Rage — combat-critical, your Vanish setup for Number 024 at the Cave to the Sealed Gate. Learned by fighting it here with Gau active; confirm it's actually banked before that stop, not just encountered","Trillium Rage (from Mt. Kolts, back before Gau joined) is combat-critical here too — Dadaluma is poison-weak and Trillium's attack is Poison Touch. Confirm it's been re-fought with Gau present since Mt. Kolts, or it isn't banked yet","Nine containers, several easy to walk past","Beating Dadaluma opens the top of the tower — Ramuh, Kirin, Siren AND Cait Sith are all sitting right there. Free, automatic, nothing to buy or unlock — not related to the Auction House at all","Whichever pub you picked Shadow up from (Kohlingen's tavern is the guaranteed one — see that stop), he joined at your CURRENT PARTY AVERAGE, not a fixed level. That average isn't just earned EXP: Gau's join back on the Veldt was party-average+2, a fixed BONUS rather than a fixed number, and it's been nudging the average up ever since. So even at a strict 0x the whole way, don't be surprised if Shadow walked in already matching everyone else — there's no guaranteed grind to do","Shadow leaves with whatever he is wearing — STRIP HIM before dropping him in Narshe","Same every time he departs; he is transient all through the World of Balance","No shops in Zozo — arrive stocked","Harvester, Hill Gigas, Veil Dancer aren't required here, but are listed too in case they turn up while you're farming Gobbledygook — also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1"],[],[29,62],[22],"",null,null,null,["Enter Zozo and talk to townsfolk for clock-time clues — everyone lies except the man just outside the Inn","Solve the clock puzzle (6:10:50) on the ground floor of the Inn-marked building to reveal the secret staircase and the Chainsaw","Sweep the town for its nine treasure chests, several of which are easy to walk past","Fight toward Dadaluma; he counters Fight, Magic, and Steal, so lean on Tools/Blitz/Bushido/Rage instead","Rage-farm Gobbledygook (needed later at the Cave to the Sealed Gate) and confirm Trillium is banked (needed for Dadaluma) while in town","Defeat Dadaluma to open the top of the tower","Collect Ramuh, Kirin, Siren, and Cait Sith automatically at the top — free, not Auction-House-related","Continue the story with Terra"]],["Opera House",1,"Stopping the weight",["Fight both rat types — Stunner (fire-weak) and Goetia (ice-weak)","Aspiran Rage (Gigavolt) helps against Ultros here — confirm it's actually banked from a Veldt trip since Serpent Trench, not just fought there, or Gau won't have it yet","SETZER joins after this sequence, once you take the Blackjack"],["g7"],[13],[],"once",null,null,null,["Perform the opera as Celes (fixed correct lines: 'Oh my hero...', 'I'm the darkness', 'Must my...')","Fight the rafter rats — Stunner (fire-weak), Goetia (ice-weak)","Continue through the following sequence and defeat Ultros (Aspiran Rage helps if it's actually banked)","Setzer joins peacefully right after — no fight is needed to recruit him, he's fooled by Celes' coin trick","Take the Blackjack to leave"]],["Southern Continent & Veldt forest",1,"",["Litwor Chicken, Joker, Don, Wyvern, Grasswyrm, Bug and Grenade are also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1","Intangir on Triangle Island once you have the airship — that one stays put, it's Gau's strongest Rage"],[],[30,31],[],"",null,null,null,["Explore the Southern Continent for story progression and any available chests","Detour to the Veldt to encounter/farm the enemies listed for bestiary completion","Note Intangir is deferred to Triangle Island once the airship is available — it stays put and is Gau's strongest Rage"]],["Albrook & Maranda",1,"",["Albrook's empty chests stay empty — they still count"],[],[],[23,24],"",[["Reflect Ring ×3",18000,"TOP PRIORITY — Albrook. You need four total; one is found in Narshe",null],["Priest's Miter ×4",12000,"magic evasion for the Ifrit/Shiva fight",null],["Hermes Sandals",7000,"Tzen — bring your total to four",null],["Mythril Mail",3500,"LOCKE, CELES and your fourth",null],["White Dress",2200,"RELM joins in Thamasa","Relm"],["Ninja Gear",1100,"SHADOW, and GAU wears it too","Shadow"],["Teleport Stone",700,"buy a stack",null]],null,null,["Visit Albrook and open both chests in the Armor Shop (they're empty but still count toward the treasure checklist)","Visit Maranda for its story beat and any chests","Continue on toward the Magitek Factory"]],["Magitek Factory (IMRF)",1,"Meeting Setzer to leave",["LEAD WITH YOUR THIRD CHARACTER — red Magna Roader will not spawn behind Locke, Edgar or Gau","No shops inside and no way back — restock Hi-Potions and Phoenix Downs before entering","No Soul Shrine in PR, so there is no second chance at it","Quicksave before the cart sequence","Grab Ifrit before leaving — it also gates Drain for everyone but Terra","Stoneblade is a hidden passage in the Research Facility","NUMBER 128 is the boss at the end of the rail-cart escape — a center body plus Left and Right Blade","Steal Kazekiri #1 from it — the Thief's Bracer doesn't exist yet at this point in the route (its only sources are a Narshe chest that opens AFTER this trip, and a Tzen shop in the World of Ruin), so this is a base-rate steal, not a boosted one. Not technically missable, but it stays this rare for a long time afterward, so it's worth resetting for if you whiff it","Ghost Rage (Thundara) helps against Number 128","Escaping Vector afterward throws two Cranes at you (both weak to Water) — Anguiform Rage's Aqua Breath (from Serpent Trench) hits both at once, confirm it's banked"],["g8","g9"],[14],[25,26],"once",null,null,["Lead with anyone EXCEPT Locke, Edgar or Gau — the red Magna Roader (X-Ether steal) won't spawn behind them"],["Restock Hi-Potions and Phoenix Downs before entering — no shops inside and no way back","Lead with your third character so the red Magna Roader spawns","Explore the Research Facility: grab Ifrit and find the hidden Stoneblade passage","Quicksave before the rail-cart escape sequence","Ride the cart escape, fighting off pursuers","Defeat Number 128 (center body plus Left and Right Blade) at the end of the escape","Steal Kazekiri #1 from Number 128 — base-rate steal, since the Thief's Bracer isn't available yet at this point in the route","Meet Setzer to leave"]],["Narshe — the return",1,"",["The locked treasure-house chest opens now","Jidoor Auction House: buy Golem and Zona Seeker (~30,000 gil) — your first +2 espers","Sleeping in the Figaro Castle beds with Edgar AND Sabin in the party triggers a bonus scene — not possible on the first visit"],[],[],[27],"",[["Figaro Castle: Drill",3000,"EDGAR — lead with him for 50% off; Flash is optional, no fight needs it",null],["Jidoor Auction House: Golem + Zona Seeker",30000,"your first +2 espers — top priority",null],["Jidoor Auction House: Seraph",3000,"optional — teaches nothing new but faster",null],["Hero's Ring is FREE",0,"Dragon's Neck cabin pot — give it to Gau",null],["Tiara",3000,"RELM joins in Thamasa","Relm"],["Poison Rod",1500,"STRAGO joins in Thamasa — first rod sold anywhere","Strago"]],null,null,["Open the previously locked treasure-house chest, now available","Detour to the Jidoor Auction House and bid on Golem (~20,000 gil) and Zona Seeker (~10,000 gil) — your first +2 espers","Handle any remaining Narshe story/shopping business","If passing through Figaro Castle with both Edgar and Sabin in the party, sleep in the beds for the bonus scene"]],["Lone Wolf",1,"Choice made",["MOG joins here","Save MOG, not Lone Wolf, or you lose a Dance"],["g10"],[],[],"once",null,null,null,["Travel to the Narshe cliffs area to trigger the Lone Wolf/Mog scene","Wait a moment — Mog knocks Lone Wolf back","Choose to save Mog (recruits him) rather than take the Gold Hairpin Lone Wolf offers"]],["Cave to the Sealed Gate",1,"Boarding the ship at Albrook",["BIGGEST TRAP — Simmeh says walk through with encounters off. Do not.","Number 024 is here — Gobbledygook Rage (Vanish) is combat-critical for it. Confirm it's actually banked from Zozo before this fight, not just encountered there","Five entries plus Ultima Weapon, Heiji's Jitte and Kazekiri #2 lock here","Eighteen containers including four hidden floor items"],["g11"],[15],[28],"wob",null,null,null,["Do not use any 'no encounters' effect here — story-critical fights and treasures require normal encounters","Work through the cave, collecting its chests including 4 hidden floor items","Grab the Assassin's Dagger, Elixir, Magicite Shards, Hi-Ether, and the Ultima Weapon in the multi-chest room","Get Heiji's Jitte from the upper-right ledge chest in the first small lava room","Cross the new bridge for the Genji Glove","Get Kazekiri #2","Reach and pass through the Sealed Gate to conclude the stop"]],["Vector & Imperial Palace",1,"Banquet end",["93 POINTS MAXIMUM — 44 from the four-minute soldier walkabout, 49 from the banquet itself","REWARDS ARE CUMULATIVE THRESHOLDS: South Figaro is liberated regardless of score / 50+ DOMA CASTLE reopens / 67+ Observation Post armory (12 chests) / 77+ the Tintinnabulum / 90+ the Ward Bangle","You need roughly 90 of 93 for all five. Treat this as a full-marks run, not a best-effort one","WALKABOUT: 24 soldiers in four minutes. 1 point each, and the four that attack you are worth 6 each if you win (the usual 1 for talking, +5 for the win) — only 1 if you lose or flee","The two Elite Soldiers in Gestahl's throne room do NOT count, and neither does Kefka in his cell — skip Kefka, he burns a large slice of the timer","Do NOT collect treasure during the timer. The palace chests stay open afterwards","Once you have all 24 you can end the timer early through a top door in the throne room","BANQUET ANSWERS: toast \"To our homelands\" (5) / \"Leave him in jail\" (5) / \"That was inexcusable\" (5)","Ask Gestahl all THREE questions, once each, 2 points apiece. Asking one twice is MINUS 10","He then asks which you asked FIRST — remember the order, correct is worth 5","Take Cid's break and beat the sentries inside the two-minute limit for 5. Fail and you score 0 for it","Then \"That your war is truly over\", and YES to boarding the ship. Saying no first forfeits the bonus even if you say yes after","On the remaining prompts pick the conciliatory option each time (e.g. trusting Terra whether she spied or not)","Tintinnabulum and Ward Bangle are GIFT rewards here, not chests — they appear nowhere else on this route","Fight the Imperial Elite via a non-Gestahl NPC after 'Take a break'","Trillium Rage, Bioblaster and Bio for that fight — same Trillium banking check as Zozo applies here"],["g12"],[16],[29,30],"once",null,null,null,["Save before entering — this is a one-shot sequence if you want full marks","During the 4-minute soldier walkabout, talk to all 24 soldiers (skip Kefka's cell and the throne-room guards — neither counts)","Let the four hostile soldiers (three normal, one armored) fight you and win them for the bonus points","Skip treasure chests during the timer — the palace chests stay open afterward","At the banquet, answer 'To our homelands,' 'Leave him in jail,' and 'That was inexcusable'","Ask Gestahl all three optional questions once each (repeating one costs 10 points), then correctly recall which you asked first","During Cid's break, fight the Imperial Elite (poison-weak) within the 2-minute limit","Answer 'That your war is truly over,' then say Yes the first time you're asked to board the ship","Collect rewards on the way out based on cumulative point thresholds"]],["Albrook — second visit",1,"",["Last chance to restock before sailing to Thamasa","Teleport Stone in a crate by the docks entrance"],[],[],[31],"",null,null,null,["Restock supplies — last chance before sailing to Thamasa","Grab the Teleport Stone from the crate near the docks entrance","Board the ship to Thamasa"]],["Thamasa & Crescent Island",1,"Before the Esper Caves",["STRAGO and RELM join here","Memento Ring is hidden upstairs in Strago's house","Five barrels around town, all gone after the Esper Caves","General Leo is a guest and does not survive — do not hand him anything you want back","Strago's Lores bypass Reflect and Runic, which pairs well with Celes","He learns a Lore by seeing it used and WINNING the fight — fleeing cancels it","Gau's Rages and Relm's Sketch/Control can teach him Lores too, not just enemies","Briareus, Devourer, Chimera are also summarized in the World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup section near the end of Act 1"],[],[32],[32],"timed",[["Shops stay shut",0,"Thamasa will not sell until the Cave to the Sealed Gate is done",null],["Ice Rod ×1 minimum",3000,"absolute minimum — required for Flame Eater",null],["Thunder Rod ×3",9000,"for the fast Ultros strategy in the Esper Cave",null],["Ice Rod ×7–8 + Flame Rod ×3–4",30000,"for a fast Typhon + Ultros on the FC approach",null],["Buy a dozen of each if flush",0,"that will last the rest of the game",null],["Mythril Rod",500,"STRAGO joins here",null],["Gaia Gear",6000,"TERRA, LOCKE, STRAGO",null]],null,null,["Explore Thamasa town and loot its five barrels before they disappear after the Esper Caves","Get the Memento Ring hidden upstairs in Strago's house (examine the wall by the table)","Strago and Relm join automatically","Proceed through the story with General Leo as a guest — he does not survive, so don't hand him anything you want back","Win (don't flee) fights against Lore-bearing enemies with Strago present to learn their Lores; Gau's Rage and Relm's Sketch/Control can also teach him Lores","Continue on to the Esper Caves"]],["Burning House",1,"Engaging Flame Eater",["Fight at least one Balloon formation","Strago joins already knowing three Lores: Aqua Breath, Revenge Blast and Stone","Aqua Breath hits ALL enemies with water — it sweeps the fire-based Balloons here","Flame Eater is fire too: Aqua Breath, or break an Ice Rod for a fast kill"],["g13"],[17],[33],"once",null,null,null,["Enter as Terra/Locke/Strago; equip Strago with an esper/relics before going in","Fight through the Balloon formations in rooms 2-5 (they come in packs of ~3, sometimes 6)","Optionally stand still against a lone Balloon and let it Self-Destruct to teach Strago the Lore","Grab the Flame Rod (room 4, right-hand door) and Ice Rod (room 5, right-hand door) chests","Equip Shiva if available before the top floor, then engage Flame Eater","Use Aqua Breath, Blizzara, or Ice Rods on Flame Eater (it's weak to Ice)","Survive the Balloon/Grenade reinforcements it summons and finish it off"]],["Triangle Island",1,"",["DO NOT fight Intangir at level 6 — its Meteor counter hits each character for 850–968","COME BACK after Gau reaches 26 in the Esper Cave, before the Floating Continent — that is the window","It starts Invisible; only a SPELL can touch it. Stop is a status weakness and deals no damage, so it does not trigger the counter","Cast Stop, damage it while frozen, and re-cast before it wears off","Hermes Sandals for auto-Haste so you act faster than the Stop timer","Non-elemental damage only — it absorbs every element. Gau's Stray Cat rage (Cat Scratch, x4) is ideal","Strago's STONE Lore does 8x damage to an enemy on the SAME level — at 26 that shreds Intangir","He knows Stone from the moment he joins, so nothing needs hunting first","Do NOT use Chainsaw: Intangir is Deathproof and Chainsaw misses 25% of the time","If it wakes with 1,280 HP or less it FLEES — no bestiary entry, so keep Stop up","Whoever lands the killing blow eats a final Meteor. Expect to lose them and still win the fight","Vanish + Doom no longer works in the Pixel Remaster"],[],[33],[],"",null,null,null,["Sail to Triangle Island and find the small forest near one tip where Intangir hides","Save before engaging; do NOT fight it while badly underleveled (its Meteor counter one-shots a low-level party)","Come back once Gau is level 26 from the Esper Cave grind, before leaving for the Floating Continent","Cast any spell on it to break Invisibility and wake it — if it wakes below ~1,280 HP it flees instead of fighting","Cycle Stop on it every couple of rounds and hit it with non-elemental damage (Gau's Cat Scratch, Strago's Stone/Traveler, Edgar's Drill)","Avoid Chainsaw's death effect (Intangir is Deathproof, so the hit just misses) and don't rely on Vanish+Doom","Land the killing blow accepting that whoever does eats one last Meteor"]],["Esper Caves",1,"Defeating Ultros (3rd time)",["Healing Rod #1 here","Ultros guards the Warring Triad statue room — his third fight. Don't use Water attacks on him, they heal him","Five entries; Bonnacons and Adamankaries are your Phase II grinding spot"],["g14"],[18],[34],"wob",null,null,null,["Enter with Terra, Locke, Strago (or preferred party) and grab the Healing Rod chest just inside","Work through Bonnacon/Adamankary inside and Land Grillon/Mandrake/Venobennu on the outside slopes","Against Venobennu pairs, hold off killing the second one so it uses Pearl Wind for Strago to learn","Reach the Warring Triad statue room and examine the statues","Fight off Ultros (his third encounter) guarding the path onward — don't use water attacks, they heal him","Backtrack through the switch-triggered trapdoor rooms for the X-Potion, Chocobo Suit, and Tabby Suit chests","Reach the Esper chamber to end the segment; you're returned to Thamasa automatically"]],["Doma Castle — later",1,"",["GATED ON THE BANQUET — the castle only reopens once the Empire withdraws, which needs 50+ points at Vector. Fall short and Doma stays shut until the World of Ruin","First three treasures also appear in Cyan's Dream if missed"],[],[],[35],"wob",null,null,null,["Confirm you scored 50+ points at the Vector banquet (Doma-withdrawal reward tier) before sailing back","Enter through the main gate; grab the Hi-Ether chest and examine the clock for an Elixir in the west rooms","Visit Cyan's family room (upper-right area) for the X-Potion chest","Follow the outer wall around to the last door for the Phoenix Down and Prayer Beads chests","If any of the first three items were missed here, they can still be picked up later in Cyan's Dream"]],["World of Balance — Act 1 Cleanup",1,"Triggering the Floating Continent",["This closes the moment you trigger the Floating Continent — treat everything below as due now, not optional","Duplicated from the story stops above so you get one consolidated last pass instead of hunting piecemeal across the whole map, which only dilutes the pool for rarer Rages you still need on the Veldt","Missable enemies, bosses, and anything wanted for a Rage are also listed at their own story stop earlier in this list — tick either copy and both update"],[],[22,23,24,25,26,5,6,8,11,27,28,29,30,31,32],[],"wob",null,true,null,["Sweep back through every earlier World of Balance stop for anything still outstanding","Prioritize any of the 9 combat-critical Rages not yet banked on the Veldt","Pick up any reachable missable bosses/chests/bestiary entries before triggering the Floating Continent","Treat this as the last call — nothing here is optional once the trigger fires"]],["END OF ACT I AUDIT",1,"Triggering the Floating Continent",["SPEND YOUR GIL FIRST — every shop in the world changes inventory or closes once Nelapa dies","The Display Map is in the MAIN MENU bestiary, not the in-game one — easy to miss","Target: 118 chests opened before the point of no return"],["g15"],[],[],"once",null,null,null,["Spend all remaining gil — shop inventories change or close once Nelapa dies","Check overall bestiary/completion % via the Display Map in the MAIN MENU (not the in-field menu)","Cross-check your open-chest count against the stated target","Trigger the Floating Continent once satisfied everything is done"]],["Esper Cave leveling",2,"",["Gau to level 26 — Esper Cave first screen, Zona Seeker equipped, EXP 4x","Why 26: the last level everyone can reach before Sabin needs a Crusader level for 999 MP","Vanish Gau first — nothing in that fight can then touch him","Dual-stat Gau: skip Bahamut and Crusader entirely, backfill Bismarck afterward","Once Gau is 26, detour to Triangle Island and kill Intangir — that is the only realistic window","Level recalculation points: Shadow at the Floating Continent, and every World of Ruin re-recruit","Nothing recalculates when the three scenarios reunite — low levels stay low through the World of Balance"],["g16"],[],[],"wob",null,null,null,["Set the EXP boost to 4x in the Config/Boost menu","Take Gau alone to the Esper Cave's first screen and grind the Bonnacon/Adamankary encounters there","Equip Zona Seeker (Magic Power +2 per level-up) and cast Vanish on Gau before each fight","Grind to level 26","While Gau is still 26, detour to Triangle Island and clear the Intangir fight (last realistic window)","Leap Gau onto the Veldt afterward so his level stops counting toward party averages"]],["Air Force",3,"Defeating the main body",["Destroy the Laser Gun and ONLY the Laser Gun so Bit spawns — CONFIRMED for PR, two independent current sources agree, none support a kill-all-adds alternative","Quicksave first as insurance","Steal X-Ether #1 from the Laser Gun"],["g17"],[19],[],"once",null,null,null,["Survive the Sky Armor/Spitfire skirmishes and the Ultros+Typhon fight on the way to the Floating Continent","Air Force immediately attacks afterward with its Laser Gun and Missile Bay parts still up","Focus fire on the Laser Gun ONLY, leaving Missile Bay alive, to make the Bit spawn","Steal the X-Ether off the Laser Gun before it dies if you want it","Kill the Bit with physical attacks only — it absorbs any magic thrown at Air Force while alive","Clean up Missile Bay and the main body (weak to Lightning/Water)"]],["Floating Continent",3,"Approaching the Statues",["DO NOT TALK TO SHADOW until Gau is safely Leaped away on the Veldt — otherwise his level 26 counts toward the average and Shadow joins higher than he needs to (see the Levels tab for why that matters)","So: clear most of the continent, jump back to the airship, Leap Gau on the Veldt, then return","STRIP GAU before you Leap him on the Veldt — his equipment goes with him and stays gone until you re-recruit him","Then recruit Shadow (joins at 6) and level HIM plus one Break-caster to 26","The Break-caster must boost the OPPOSITE stat to Shadow — you have Shadow on Magic, so pick a Strength character (Celes)","Kill all but one enemy, KO everyone except those two, then finish the fight","During the LEVELLING grind, run from Ninjas and Dragons — Break does not work on them. Kill one of each separately for the bestiary.","Once Shadow is done, level everyone else to 26 wherever you like","Eight bestiary entries here; four orb containers, one is a Gigantos fight (Bio kills it in one turn)"],["g18"],[20],[36],"wob",null,null,["Level Shadow (joins at 6) plus one Strength Break-caster (Celes) to 26 here — everyone else can free-ride to 26 later, wherever you like"],["Land near the save point, use it, then recruit Shadow and re-equip him (he's stripped except his esper)","Explore the map, fighting Apokrypha/Behemoth/Brainpan/Misfit/Ninja/Platinum Dragon/Dragon and clearing the mandatory Gigantos fight (drops the Sasuke orb)","Before finishing the whole map, jump back to the airship and Leap Gau onto the Veldt (strip his gear first) so his level doesn't inflate the party average","Talk to Shadow — he joins at the current party average, now lower without Gau counted","Grind Shadow plus one opposite-stat Break-caster (e.g. Celes if Shadow's on Magic) to level 26 using Break/kill-most-then-finish tactics","Run from Ninja and Dragon during the grind (Break/Petrify doesn't land on either) but still clear one of each once for the bestiary","Level the rest of the active roster to 26, then proceed toward Ultima Weapon and the point of no return"]],["Floating Continent — escape",3,"Jumping to the Blackjack",["Naude must be KILLED — Imp makes them flee and registers nothing","Six-minute timer; Fire, Lightning or Holy","Wait at the jump point for Shadow","If you jump without Shadow you lose him AND everything he is carrying until the World of Ruin Coliseum"],["g19"],[21],[],"once",null,null,null,["Celes joins (if not already present); the six-minute escape timer starts","Fight through the Naude formations — actually kill at least one rather than Imp-ing it into fleeing, for the bestiary entry","Use Fire/Lightning/Holy-elemental attacks or Rasp on Naude (KO-based attacks miss them)","Grab the Elixir orb by approaching from the south/east, not directly (the direct path collapses)","Defeat Nelapa (weak to Ice/Lightning/Holy, absorbs Fire) — offense only, the timer keeps running","Reach the jump point and wait there for Shadow instead of jumping immediately","Jump to the Blackjack once Shadow appears (around the 0:04 mark)"]],["Solitary Island & Southern Continent",4,"",["LEVEL AVERAGING — the rule that governs the whole World of Ruin","Anyone you re-recruit is set to the AVERAGE of your current members, rounded down","It never lowers a level, only raises it — so a straggler gets dragged up with no esper attached","So: FIND EVERYONE FIRST, then start levelling. Keep EXP at 0x until the roster is complete.","Fish for Cid — fast fish keep him alive, slow ones do not"],[],[34,35],[],"",null,null,null,["Land in the World of Ruin; before leveling anyone, prioritize tracking down and recruiting the rest of the cast","Keep the EXP boost low/off while the roster is still incomplete","Recruit each character, accepting that under-leveled ones get pulled up to the current party average (never down)","Once everyone is recruited, resume normal leveling/EXP boosts","At Solitary Island, fish and feed Cid only fast-moving fish — slow ones (and not feeding him at all) let his condition worsen and he dies"]],["Tzen — Collapsing House",4,"Helping the child",["TIMED. Eight containers plus three entries, all lost when you help the kid","Two chests are 4x Nightwalker fights"],["g20"],[36],[37],"timed",[["Thief's Bracer",3000,"Locke — raises steal rate, needed for Kazekiri",null],["Alarm Earring",7000,"no back attacks",null],["Dragoon Boots",9000,"Mog",null],["Burning Fist",10000,"Sabin",null]],null,null,["Enter Tzen; an earthquake cutscene reveals Sabin holding up a collapsing house with a kid trapped inside","Before entering, equip a Ribbon or Jeweled Ring on Celes — some enemies inside can Petrify, and a solo Petrify is a game over (buy a Jeweled Ring at the Relic Shop if needed)","Step to the door to start the 6-minute timer (it pauses on menu/map screens) and go in alone as Celes","Clear the 8 chests: Healing Rod, Holy Rod, Ether, Hyper Wrist, two Monster-in-a-Box fights vs 4 Nightwalkers each, Blood Sword, Magicite Shard — multi-target Fira clears the Nightwalker/Zokka fights fast","Reach the basement, talk to the kid, then get both of you back outside before time runs out","The house collapses behind you; Sabin and Celes reunite and he joins the party for good","Optional: buy the Seraph esper for 10 Gil from the man behind the Relic Shop if you skipped it in the World of Balance"]],["Nikeah & Serpent Trench (WoR)",4,"",["CORRECTED: the Angler Whelk fight is not here — it's a monster-in-a-box in Darill's Tomb, see that stop instead"],["g21"],[37],[],"",[["Gale Hairpin",8000,"more preemptive strikes — helps bestiary sweeps",null],["Hyper Wrist",8000,"Strength boost",null],["Prayer Beads",4000,"Evasion +20",null],["Zephyr Cloak",7000,"evasion",null],["Angel Ring",8000,"auto-Regen",null],["Rune Blade",7500,"Celes",null]],null,null,["From Tzen, cross the bridge east/north onto the Serpent Trench — it's above ground now and walkable on foot","Fight through Trench encounters (Black Dragon, Delta Beetle, Vampire Thorn, Lizard, Devoahan — mostly Fire-weak); Sabin's Rising Phoenix clears groups quickly","Mobliz sits partway along the Trench — detour there before continuing (see next stop)","Continue the Trench to its far end to reach Nikeah","Shop Nikeah's refreshed gear (Rune Blade, Enhancer, elemental swords, new relics)","Visit the Pub, talk to the thieves, then tail their leader \"Gerad\" (Edgar in disguise) to the docks and stow away for South Figaro"]],["Mobliz (WoR) — first visit",4,"",["Do this BEFORE sailing for Figaro — you are already on this continent, and Edgar is not needed","Bring SABIN. Celes alone makes the Humbaba fight genuinely dangerous","Free healing: sleep in the abandoned Relic shop at the north of town first","Phoenix Down in a barrel by the ruined house west of the kid's house","Follow the boy into the old post office and downstairs to find Terra. She will refuse to join","Leave, and Humbaba attacks. TERRA FIGHTS HIM ALONE AND MUST LOSE — she is unequipped and cannot hurt him. Let her be KO'd","Your party then takes over. Humbaba is weak to BIO and poison, and ABSORBS lightning","Beat him and he flees; a kid then runs up and hands you the FENRIR magicite — a free esper this early is worth the trip alone","Terra still refuses. You must leave the town entirely and come back with the FALCON"],[],[],[38],"",null,null,["MUST: Sabin — Celes alone makes Humbaba genuinely dangerous"],["Enter Mobliz; grab the Phoenix Down from the barrel cluster near the ruined house, and note the free bed in the abandoned Relic Shop","Follow the kid into the messenger's house (the old post office) and down to the basement","Talk to the kids and to Terra — she refuses to fight","Before leaving, equip Sabin with Venom Claws (dual + Genji Glove if you have them) and Quick Save","Leave the house — Terra confronts Humbaba alone and is meant to lose; she's unequipped and cannot hurt him, so just let her be KO'd","Celes and Sabin take over: use Poison/Bio damage, avoid any Thunder-based spells (Humbaba absorbs Lightning and heals from it)","Deal roughly 7500 damage and Humbaba flees; a kid runs up afterward and gives you the Fenrir magicite","Terra still refuses to join — leave town entirely; her recruitment arc resumes only after you have the Falcon"]],["Figaro Continent & South Figaro (WoR)",4,"",["LAST CHANCE on the South Figaro outdoor containers and cave chests","Figaro Castle basement opens now — five chests plus a Soul Sabre found by searching the throne-room statue","MANDATORY: fight the 4 Tentacles (bestiary #297-300) blocking the Engine Room before Edgar rejoins — he goes in completely unequipped, so gear everyone else well"],[],[38,39],[39,40,41],"",[["Hermes Sandals",7000,"second copy",null],["Diamond Armor",15000,"front-liners",null],["Diamond Helm",8000,"front-liners — pairs with Diamond Armor",null],["Gold Lance",12000,"Mog",null]],null,null,["Take the thief ferry from Nikeah to South Figaro; grab any outdoor barrels/boxes you skipped in the World of Balance (10 containers, contents refreshed for WoR)","Visit South Figaro Cave and refresh its 3 chests if you missed them earlier","Follow \"Gerad\" and the thieves through the cave to the hidden passage leading into Figaro Castle's basement","Loot the B3F alcove chests (Crystal Helm, Gravity Rod, X-Potion, Hi-Ether) and the Royal Crown chest upstairs","Gear up (Reflect Rings + Hermes Sandals recommended) and fight the 4 Tentacles blocking the Engine Room — Edgar himself is unequipped for this fight","Edgar reveals himself and joins; search the throne-room statue for the hidden Soul Sabre","Ride the castle to the surface (it resurfaces at Kohlingen) to continue"]],["Kohlingen Continent",4,"",["Setzer's gambling weapons are sold here — Dice, then Viper Darts","Enhancer for Celes boosts her Magic","Four bestiary entries across the plains and forests","FIXED DICE is in Kefka's Tower but only a few rooms in — a common tactic is an early raid to grab it, then leave","Damage = die x die x die x LEVEL x 2, ignoring defence and the Master's Scroll penalty entirely"],[],[40],[],"",[["Dice",5000,"Setzer",null],["Viper Darts",13000,"Setzer — better than Dice",null],["Enhancer",10000,"Celes — boosts Magic",null]],null,null,["Land on the Kohlingen continent and fight the local bestiary entries — Bogy, Marchosias, Deepeye, and Mousse in the plains/forest, plus Sandhorse and Cancer if you head into the desert","Shop Kohlingen: Dice (5000 Gil) is cheap and has a near-term use, Viper Darts (13000 Gil) is a strong but not-yet-needed weapon, and an Enhancer (10000 Gil) is worth grabbing for a caster's Magic stat","Head to the Inn/Pub to find and recruit Setzer","Note for later: the Fixed Dice sits only a few rooms into Kefka's Tower — a common tactic is an early raid just to grab it, then leave"]],["Darill's Tomb",4,"",["TOMBSTONE PUZZLE — the phrase is THE WORLD IS SQUARE. Reward: the hidden room holding the Growth Egg on B3","FIRST examine all FOUR gravestones in the southern room, or the lone tomb will not offer the carving option","Then take the north-west door and carve. Sources disagree on the exact group order — WEHT / DLRO / QSSI / ERAU, or THEW / ORLD / ISSQ / UARE — so just arrange whatever groups it offers to spell the phrase","The Growth Egg room is off the Regal Gown room: south-east corner, walk east into the wall","Growth Egg is behind a hidden path east of the Regal Gown","Angler Whelk monster-in-a-box north-west of the save point: kill the head AND shell simultaneously for 2 Dragon Claws instead of 1 — Fandom says PR may always drop 2 regardless of kill method, but the PR-specific GameFAQs walkthrough still describes the old simultaneous-kill requirement, so treat the double-drop as not guaranteed and go for the simultaneous kill anyway","Dullahan guards the tomb exit to the Falcon — mandatory fight, opens with a one-shot Lv.? Holy targeting anyone whose level divides evenly into your current Gil's last digit, and punishes worn Reflect Rings with status ailments, so take them off first","No shop here — it is a tomb. Stock up in Maranda after you take the Falcon"],[],[41],[42],"",null,null,null,["Equip Ribbons/Amulets before entering — most enemies here are undead and several use Zombie/instant-death effects","B1: optional Borghese fight (only found in this room)","B2: work the 6-door puzzle — grab the Crystal Mail and Regal Gown chests, then take the hidden path off the Regal Gown room for the Growth Egg","Examine all four southern gravestones (ERAU / QSSI / DLRO / WEHT) first, or the lone NW tombstone won't offer to carve","Carve WEHT DLRO QSSI ERAU (\"THE WORLD IS SQUARE\" backwards) and grab the Genji Helm chest","Use the turtles to cross to the save point; fight the Angler Whelk monster-in-a-box for Dragon Claw(s), then grab the Man-Eater chest","Heal up, remove any Reflect Rings, and fight Dullahan guarding Darill's tomb","Follow Setzer down through the memory sequence to find the Falcon airship"]],["Maranda (WoR)",4,"",["Reachable once you have the FALCON. Celes points you here straight after Darill's Tomb","Talk to LOLA, who has been reading letters from her boyfriend in Mobliz","Talk to the dove afterwards and it flies to Zozo — that is where the letters come from","In Zozo, buy the RUST-RID (1000 gil, from a man near the Inn) to open the roof door to Mt. Zozo and Cyan","Best armour on sale anywhere at this point in the game"],[],[],[],"",[["Crystal Shield",7000,"Maranda WoR",null],["Magus Robe",13000,"best caster robe",null],["Crystal Mail",17000,"best heavy armour buyable",null]],null,null,["Land near Maranda now that you have the Falcon — Celes points you here right after Darill's Tomb","Talk to the ex-thief in the Inn and the woman between the shops for flavor hints","Buy from the refreshed weapon/armor stock (Crystal Mail, Crystal Shield, Falchion, elemental scrolls, Tao Robe, Dark Gear) — the strongest gear on sale anywhere up to this point","Talk to Lola; read her latest letter and agree to write back, receiving the Lola's Letter key item","Give the letter to the pigeon outside; watch it fly off toward Zozo, which is where the letters have been coming from","Optional: fight in the desert south of town for early Cactuar/Slagworm Gil and Magic AP"]],["Mobliz (WoR) — return for Terra",4,"",["REQUIRES THE FALCON — you cannot trigger this on foot, so it waits until after Darill's Tomb","Speak to the kids, then enter the house on the WEST side of town","A dog follows you in and reveals a secret chamber behind the bookcase","Hi-Ether in a pot down there before you go back out","Head outside for Humbaba round two — same weaknesses (Poison) and absorption (Lightning), but CORRECTED: it's actually two more back-to-back fights (he heals to full mid-scene when Terra joins), needing roughly triple the damage of the first Mobliz encounter, not just 'slightly stronger'","Part way through he blows two of your party out of the fight and TERRA joins in Esper form, double attack and defence","Beat him and Terra rejoins permanently"],[],[],[46],"",null,null,null,["Fly the Falcon back to Mobliz once you have it — this scene does not trigger on foot","Head to the messenger's house basement; learn that Katarin is missing","Enter the house to the west (Duane the wounded soldier's house); follow the dog behind the bookcase to find Katarin and Terra","Grab the Hi-Ether from the pot before leaving","Equip Thunder protection (Force Armor / Thunder Shield / Reflect Ring) and load up on Bio/Poison damage","Leave the house — Humbaba attacks again; whittle him down (weak to Poison, absorbs Lightning) until he uses Humbaba Breath, ejecting two party members","Terra enters in Trance form and Humbaba heals back to full — finish him off for good this time","Terra rejoins permanently; equip her with Relics and an Esper before moving on"]],["Mt. Zozo",4,"",["Five chests on the way up: Ice Shield, Red Cap, Thunder Shield, Aegis Shield, Gold Hairpin","Cyan's locked chest gives Books the first time, then is empty — both count","MANDATORY: Storm Dragon guards the way back out (weak to Lightning, guaranteed Force Armor drop) — do NOT wear the Ice Shield chest you just picked up, its wind attacks double the wearer's damage taken"],[],[42],[43],"",null,null,null,["In Zozo town, buy Rust-Rid (1000 Gil) from the man near the Inn","Use it on the rusted door atop the building marked \"Pub\" to open the path up to Mt. Zozo","Consider casting Vanish/Phantom before entering — nearly every regular enemy here is a high-evasion physical attacker (a Sniper Eye also works)","Work through the cave picking up 5 chests: Ice Shield, Red Cap, Thunder Shield, Aegis Shield, Gold Hairpin — do NOT equip the Ice Shield for the boss fight (Storm Dragon's wind attacks double its wearer's damage)","Reach Cyan's hiding spot; read his confession letter to Lola; the locked chest gives Books the first time, then reads empty on a second search (both count)","Cyan joins; if you want him in your active party, you'll need to backtrack to the Falcon and return","Back at the save point, gear up (Thunder Shield is safe here, avoid the Ice Shield) and fight the Storm Dragon (weak to Lightning) for a guaranteed Force Armor"]],["Cave on the Veldt",4,"",["Berserker Ring chest, then Death Warden monster-in-a-box through the northwest hidden passage for a Tigerfang","Ichigeki chest before the section-3 switch — this is Shadow's ultimate weapon, don't sell it","MANDATORY: Living Behemoth King, then an ambush from its Undead form right after — stay invisible (Vanish/Phantom) the whole approach"],[],[43],[44],"",null,null,null,["Enter the cave on the southwest side of the Veldt; follow Interceptor in","Grab the Berserker Ring chest, then take the hidden-path detour to the Death Warden monster-in-a-box for a Tigerfang","Grab the Ichigeki chest before flipping the section-3 switch — this is Shadow's ultimate weapon, don't sell it","Stay invisible (Vanish/Phantom) all the way to the save point; equip Reflect Rings if you have them","Fight the Living Behemoth King (an Imp spell trivializes it while you're invisible), then the Undead Behemoth King that ambushes immediately after","You'll automatically fly the injured Shadow (or Relm, depending on your Floating Continent choice) to Thamasa afterward"]],["Owzer's Mansion",4,"Defeating Chadarnook",["The mansion is DARK and a voice blocks the stairs — examine the CANDELABRA at the foot of the staircase to turn the lights on","That also reveals Owzer's diary, which is the hint you are meant to get","FLOWER painting, north-east corner — fight Rafflesia. Fire kills it fast. This is the one that vanishes forever when the dungeon ends","GESTAHL portrait, west side — examine it TWICE for the Emperor's Letter, which reveals the Phoenix Cave location","Painting in the SOUTH-WEST corner — fight two Misty. Rare steal: Moogle Suit","STILL LIFE painting — kill it with Fire to open the hidden door. Rare steal: Fake Mustache, which turns Sketch into Control","Nearly every enemy here has an animal-suit rare steal — those chain into Genji Armor at the Coliseum","The four floating chests each start a fight when you stand under their shadow: 293 Gil, Potion, Ether, Gold Needle","Before talking to Owzer for the Chadarnook fight, equip LIGHTNING and SLEEP protection"],["g22"],[44],[45],"once",[["Jidoor's WoR shops",0,"The mansion is IN Jidoor — these are the town's shelves, not the dungeon's",null],["Circlet",7000,"Jidoor's shops, right outside the mansion — big Magic boost",null],["Black Cowl",7500,"Shadow / Locke",null],["Crystal Helm",10000,"Jidoor's shops, right outside the mansion — best helm on sale",null],["Black Garb",13000,"Shadow, Locke and Gogo",null]],null,null,["First pass (any time after recruiting Gau): try the stairs — a voice warns you off and Owzer's diary appears; examine the candelabra/lamp at the foot of the stairs to light the mansion and proceed","Examine the Flower painting for a mandatory Rafflesia fight — this is missable, it can't be triggered again once Chadarnook is defeated","Examine the Gestahl portrait twice for the Emperor's Letter, revealing the Phoenix Cave's location","Ignore the SW woman painting for now — you'll come back to it","Second pass (after recruiting Shadow at the Coliseum): examine the SW woman painting for the 2x Misty fight (Moogle Suit steal)","Push through the chair-painting ambush, then grab the Moogle Suit chest and the hidden Lich Ring chest","Fight the shadow-triggered encounters under all 4 floating chests (293 Gil, Potion, Ether, Gold Needle)","Examine the armor portrait for the Still Life fight (Fake Mustache steal), which opens the boss door","Equip Lightning and Sleep protection, talk to Owzer, and defeat Chadarnook (target its Demon form, avoid attacking the Lakshmi form)","Get the Lakshmi magicite from the bookcase; Relm joins the party"]],["Phoenix Cave",4,"",["You need the Emperor's Letter from Owzer's first — the cave is where the mountains form a STAR, north of the southern continent near Tzen. Land in the gap at its centre","Split into TWO parties of four. Party 1 fights the boss, so stack it","The switch puzzle is long but LINEAR — swap control each time a party reaches a dead end or a switch","Enemies here Zombify and some open with Death — bring Amulets or Ribbons, and the Lich Ring from Owzer's makes Death heal instead","The hook at the entrance takes you back to the Falcon if you want out mid-puzzle","Five of the nine chests are empty and still count. The Phoenix chest cannot be opened any other way"],[],[45],[52],"",null,null,null,["Land at the star-shaped mountain gap (its location comes from the Emperor's Letter found at Owzer's) and split into two parties","Work the long but linear switch puzzle, swapping control at each dead end/switch; grab the Teleport Stone, Wing Edge, Ribbon, and Dragon Horn chests — 5 others in the dungeon are empty but still count toward the total","Regroup your strongest party, gear up in Fire resistance (or Rasp to strip its MP), and fight the Red Dragon (weak to Ice/Water) for a Murakumo","Trigger the two remaining floor switches (one per party) to open the final path","Follow the path to find Locke and the Phoenix Magicite — the scene auto-continues to Kohlingen","In Kohlingen, watch the Rachel scene: Locke joins, you get the Phoenix esper, and he hands over everything that was in the 'empty' chests (X-Potion, Phoenix Down, X-Ether, Elixir, Flame Shield, Valiant Knife)"]],["Narshe (WoR) & Umaro's cave",4,"",["The three upgraded Mines chests — Guard Bracelet, Elixir, Ribbon — no source found suggests these ever lock out, so 'last chance' isn't the actual pressure here; just don't forget them","Molulu's Charm is hidden behind where Mog stood","CURSED SHIELD: equip it and win 256 battles (not 255) to turn it into the Paladin's Shield — the on-screen message appears right after, which is what caused the off-by-one figure","Cultists' Tower fights, Coliseum fights, and any battle whose results screen gets skipped (Gau Leaping, everyone fleeing) do NOT count toward the 256 — don't expect to double-dip","It inflicts every bad status while cursed — park it on someone durable and grind normally","The Paladin's Shield teaches ULTIMA, which is your replacement for the Ragnarok magicite"],[],[48],[47,48],"",null,null,null,["Arrive in Narshe, World of Ruin, with Locke in the party (required to unlock certain doors/scenes)","In the house up the stairs to the right of the Relic shop, talk to the sick old man to receive the Cursed Shield","In the Mines, search the wall where Mog once stood for Molulu's Charm","Open the three now-upgraded chests near the west mine entrance for a Ribbon, Guard Bracelet, and Elixir","Equip the Cursed Shield on whoever will carry it and start grinding battles toward the curse-lift (Solitary Island's wasteland, with a Ribbon equipped, is the recommended fast spot)","Continue on to Umaro's cave (Yeti's Cave) as the next stop"]],["Dinosaur Forest & WoR overworld",4,"",["Brachiosaur and Tyrannosaur in the forest","Brachiosaur is the best magicite AP farm in the game"],[],[46,47],[],"",null,null,null,["Travel to the dinosaur-shaped forest north of the Veldt on the WoR overworld","Fight random encounters for Tyrannosaur and Brachiosaur, both of which give large EXP","Use these fights (with the right Magicite equipped) as an AP-farming spot for learning spells quickly","Optionally try to Steal a Ribbon from Brachiosaur"]],["Yeti's Cave",4,"",["Umaro joins here; Tonberries hit hard for this point in the run"],[],[49],[],"",null,null,null,["Enter Yeti's Cave (near Narshe) with Mog in the party","Fight through Tonberry encounters on the way in — a chest here triggers a fight against 3 Tonberries (small chance of a Minerva Bustier drop)","Push through to the Midgardsormr magicite","Taking the magicite triggers a fight against Umaro, who is protective of it","Defeat Umaro; with Mog present he joins the party afterward"]],["Triangle Island (WoR) — Zone Eater & Gogo's lair",4,"",["Zone Eater sits on Triangle Island — the same island Intangir used in the World of Balance","Walk into it and let it swallow you; that is the only way in to Gogo","Six entries inside the belly, plus Zone Eater itself outside","Nine chests down the bridges and under the falling roof","GOGO joins at the end"],[],[50,52],[50],"",null,null,null,["Travel to Triangle Island (the same island Intangir occupied in the WoB)","Fight the Zone Eater (optionally kill one first for its own bestiary entry), then let it Inhale your whole party to be swallowed","Explore Zone Eater's Belly across three sub-floors (B1-B3), using the bridge-hopping and falling-ceiling puzzle rooms","Collect all 9 chests (Hi-Ether, Red Jacket, Genji Armor, Magical Brush, Fake Mustache, Zephyr Cloak, Hero's Ring, Pinwheel, Thunder Shield)","Fight the six unique enemy formations inside for their bestiary entries (Covert, Kamui, Wartpuck, Shambling Corpse, Amduscias, Baalzephon)","Reach the door at the end and talk to Gogo to recruit him","Leave via Teleport/Teleport Stone (or walk out) once done"]],["Crescent Island (WoR)",4,"",["Three entries here — Vasegiatta, Gloomwind, Purusa"],[],[51],[],"",null,null,null,["Travel to Crescent Island (Thamasa's island) in the World of Ruin","Fight random encounters around the island to log its three exclusive bestiary entries: Vasegiatta, Gloomwind, Purusa","Optionally bank Purusa's Rage (Land Slide, no elemental weakness) for Gau if he's in the party"]],["Cyan's Dream",4,"Defeating Wrexsoul",["The entire zone vanishes when Wrexsoul dies — everything below goes with it","ELEVEN entries in one closable zone — the largest loss available in the World of Ruin","Doma Castle treasures can still be collected here if missed","Steal Memento Ring #3 from Wrexsoul"],["g24"],[53],[49],"once",null,null,null,["Bring Cyan (mandatory) and at least one Steal-capable character (missable Steal coming up), then enter Doma Castle in the WoR and save outside first","Take a nap in the bedroom to trigger the Dreamscape","Work through doors A-E of the Dreamscape to reassemble your party, fighting Alluring Rider, Weredragon, Coco, Pandora, and Parasite along the way (last chance for Alluring Rider/Weredragon)","Defeat the Dream Stooges boss trio (Curlax, Laragorn, Moebius) — you must actually kill Laragorn, not just have him flee, for his bestiary entry","Continue through the dream Phantom Train and Magitek Armor cave sections, fighting Al Jabr, Io, Pluto Armor, and Schmidt (all last-chance encounters)","In the dream Doma Castle, grab any real-castle treasures still missing (they carry over) and proceed to the throne room","Steal the Memento Ring from Wrexsoul during the boss fight, then defeat him outright (do not Banish/Snort/Odin him away or he won't log in the bestiary)","Collect the Masamune and the Alexander Esper before leaving — the whole dream zone and its exclusive bestiary entries vanish once Wrexsoul is dead"]],["Ancient Castle",4,"",["Do NOT run from Samurai Soul — loses Master's Scroll AND the entry","Eleven containers across one cave (three connected sections) and the castle"],["g23"],[54],[51],"",null,null,null,["Ride Figaro Castle underground (Edgar leading gives half-price shopping) and choose to stop exploring when the castle gets stuck","Go to the jail; find the hidden doorway in the back of a cell leading into the connecting cave","Work through the cave's three sections, collecting its 6 chests and beating the Master Tonberry monster-in-a-box","Enter the Ancient Castle; defeat the Samurai Soul monster-in-a-box for the Master's Scroll — never run from this fight","Examine the petrified Odin statue in the throne room for the Odin magicite, and grab the castle's remaining 4 chests plus the X-Ether item","Trigger the hidden staircase near the queen's throne to reach and defeat the Blue Dragon","Examine the petrified queen to upgrade Odin into Raiden (irreversible), then walk back to Figaro Castle (no Teleport out)"]],["Cultists' Tower",4,"",["MAGIC ONLY — no Attack, Steal, Sketch, Lore or Rage anywhere in the tower. CORRECTED: Items ARE allowed (and needed for healing) — only Magic, Summon, Mimic and Umaro's berserk attacks are the other permitted commands. Bring casters and plenty of MP","There is a hidden room on the FIRST ascent (examine the wall by the Safety Bit chest), not a '6th floor' — the tower has no numbered floors, just four ascents","Six chests, one per storeroom floor; CORRECTED: Soul of Thamasa is a chest in the top-floor penthouse, picked up BEFORE the Magic Master fight — beating Magic Master itself gives a Megalixir"],[],[55],[53],"",null,null,null,["Assemble a strong all-magic party (ideally your four best mages, e.g. Terra/Celes/Relm/Strago; Umaro can also fight normally here, or use Gogo mimicking Magic if short a caster)","Equip for Magic/Magic Defense/Magic Evasion (physical stats don't matter) and cast Float before entering — Quake shows up often","Climb the tower's four ascents, grabbing the hidden-room chests on the way (Safety Bit, Air Anchor via a secret room found by examining a wall on the first ascent, Genji Shield, Kagenui, Force Armor)","Defeat the Holy Dragon monster-in-a-box partway up (Silence shuts it down completely) for the Holy Lance","At the top, take the Soul of Thamasa from the chest before the final fight","Defeat Magic Master (Reraise + Reflect Ring stalling, or draining its MP, are the standard plans) for a Megalixir","Fight your way back down and out (no Teleport inside the tower)"]],["Ebot's Rock",4,"",["Learn Hidon's lore; chests here refill with Coral"],[],[56],[58],"",null,null,null,["Reach Ebot's Rock and step on the floor switches, which teleport you semi-randomly around the cave","Open chests along the way — each holds 1-5 pieces of Coral, and chests refill every time you're teleported, so Coral can be farmed indefinitely","Find the hungry statue/chest and feed it 22 Coral all at once (partial feeds are simply consumed without progress) to unlock the way forward","Push on to Hidon; defeat its Erebus escorts first so Hidon uses Grand Delta, the only way to learn that Lore"]],["Coliseum",4,"",["Siegfried appears here","Wagered wins do NOT register formations for the Veldt, only the bestiary"],[],[57],[],"",null,null,null,["Reach the Coliseum north of Kohlingen — it only opens for betting in the WoR (in the WoB you can still grab the Hero's Ring from a pot outside)","Save before every bet: Coliseum fights are strictly auto-battle (no manual control), so even 'safe' bets can be lost to bad luck","Use the Coliseum Bet Table to plan chains toward specific rewards (e.g., bet Ragnarok against Daedalus for the Lightbringer)","Fight Siegfried if going for his (tough) optional bestiary entry","Treat Coliseum wins as bestiary-only — they don't register the formation for Gau's Veldt/Rage-learning purposes"]],["Ragnarok",4,"Choice made",["Narshe weapon shop, World of Ruin, with LOCKE in the party — choose SWORD or MAGICITE, never both","TAKE THE SWORD: betting it at the Coliseum is the only way to get the Lightbringer, the best weapon in the game","COST: the Ragnarok magicite is the only esper that teaches ULTIMA","Cover for that by uncursing the Cursed Shield — the Paladin's Shield it becomes also teaches Ultima","PR closed the old loophole: items stolen in the final battle are NOT kept when you save after the ending, so Ragnarok cannot be farmed. One sword, one Lightbringer.","The magicite's Metamorphose summon is also the item-farming tool — you are giving that up too"],["g25"],[],[],"once",null,null,null,["With Locke in the party, visit the weapon shop in Narshe, World of Ruin, and talk to the shopkeeper","Choose SWORD (melt the magicite into the Ragnarok sword) or MAGICITE (keep it as an Esper that teaches Ultima) — never both","If you took the sword: bet it against Daedalus at the Coliseum to win the Lightbringer, the best sword in the game","If you took the magicite: equip it to teach Ultima directly","Either way, recover the missing Ultima source later via the Cursed Shield -> Paladin's Shield grind, which also teaches Ultima","Do not plan around stealing extra Ragnaroks from Lady in the final battle — PR discards items stolen there once you save after the ending"]],["Kefka's Tower",4,"Final battle",["No shops inside — stock Megalixirs and X-Potions first","Steal Force Armor #4 from Guardian","Learn Force Field from Fiend — no other enemy uses it","Sixteen chests split across the three parties, plus a hidden Ribbon"],["g26"],[58],[54,55,56,57],"",null,null,null,["Stock up on Megalixirs/X-Potions before entering — there are no shops inside","Split your 12 strongest characters into three balanced parties (put Strago in Party 1 for a later exclusive Lore, and keep Steal-capable characters like Locke and Gogo in different parties)","Work each party's path, switching between them at the marked points, collecting the tower's 16 chests along the way","Steal the Force Armor from the Guardian boss — it's limited in quantity and won't be offered again","Have Strago learn Force Field from the Fiend boss — she's the only enemy in the game who uses it","Clear the remaining Legendary Dragon and 'statue' bosses (Guardian, Demon, Fiend, Goddess) to reunite the parties","Proceed to the final battle against Kefka"]]];
